{
  "category": "Sharp Claw Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "They live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "It sends signals to others by carving odd patterns in frost- covered trees and ice.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in snowy regions. It carves patterns in trees with its claws as a signal to others.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in snowy regions. It carves patterns in trees with its claws as a signal to others.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "They communicate by clawing signs in boulders and work together to surround enemies.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "They communicate by clawing signs in boulders and work together to surround enemies.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in snowy regions. It carves patterns in trees with its claws as a signal to others.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "They live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "It lives in snowy regions. It carves patterns in trees with its claws as a signal to others.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "They live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "They travel in groups of four or five, leaving signs for one another on trees and rocks. They bring down their prey with coordinated attacks.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "They dwell in cold places. This Pokémon’s main food source in Alola is Vulpix and Sandshrew, which they carefully divide among their group.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "One Weavile will trip a Sandshrew and flip it over, and then another Weavile will deal the finishing blow with its sharp claws.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thanks to its increased intelligence, scrapping over food is a thing of the past. A scratch from its claws will give you a case of frostbite!",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "They attack their quarry in packs. Prey as large as Mamoswine easily fall to the teamwork of a group of Weavile.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "With its claws, it leaves behind signs for its friends to find. The number of distinct signs is said to be over 500.",
      "version": "shield"
    },
    {
      "text": "This species corners prey as a pack, under the guidance of a leader. Weavile displays increased cunning, leading me to speculate that its evolution caused further brain development.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
  ],
